hings that would help  which europe generally doing france  germany um austria italy are vaccine  passports or test passports doesn't have  to be a vaccine but you know we all use  an oyster card when we get on the tube  why we can't just flash our phone and  show that we are either doubly  vaccinated or clear of covered to go  into something i don't know but if not  it will have to be working from home  which apparently is going to have the  biggest impact  yeah um and ali um  where do you where do you stand on plan  b is is it inevitable that more  restrictions are going to come in do you  think  well hopefully not and i think that the  the government is seeing that the the  way to avoid plan b is to ramp up the  the booster shot regime and that's why  uh there's a lot of pressure jeremy hunt  came up with this proposal to reduce the  time lapse between your second and third  booster jab from six months to five  months which is something that boris  johnson seems to be also in favor of uh  so i think that's really the focus and  this is also being reported that now  under 50s are going to be allowed to  have their booster jab after christmas  so i think the government's very much  seen that as the route out of this but  look um it's keeping all options on the  table we just don't know how it's going  to evolve uh you can see certain  councils liverpool council has already  broken ranks yeah encouraging people to  work from home but the government has  going to look at this in the round it's  also going to keep in mind the effects  on the economy here as well okay we've  got to head to a break uh stay where you  are uh coming up we'll discuss a story  that's on the front of the sunday  telegraph family to accompany the queen  to all events is there headline talk  about that and more in a couple minutes  [Music]  welcome back christina and ali uh still  with us um christine i'm gonna let you  start with this because i know you'll be  spitting feathers over the front