ally think that the  government is very serious particularly  boris johnson himself  is very serious about climate change i  mean you've had three different uh  documents coming out of the government  in the last few weeks on climate change  you had the net zero uh plan last week  you had uh the  the net recovery plan from the  chancellor you had the heat and building  strategies there's a lot going on but i  do think that there's a serious concern  and a bit of a division between certain  members of the cabin it looks like alok  sharma is getting a little bit upset  that boris has been over egging the  pudding about how important this is  going to be and and and  really ramping up the rhetoric on on the  cop 26 meeting uh but you've also then  got the potential issue of president xi  of china not turning up and the indians  saying that they still want to use coal  for many many years to come so it's not  going to be easy but i do think that um  it is an important thing for the  government so i wouldn't dismiss it i do  think it is a close to the top of the  agenda okay we'll find out more of  course in the coming days and finally  i'm sorry you're embarrassed about being  british christina it does does upset me  a little bit but here's something to be  proud of and that is uh the queen  um 95 years old uh resting up at the  moment but the telegraph saying that her  family are going to accompany her uh to  future events so that if she does have  to um take some time out that whoever  she's visiting won't be disappointed  well i do absolutely adore the queen i  will say that i'm a massive fan of hers  i think she's she's a symbol of  everything that's good about this  country or used to be good about this  country in that she has this incredibly  strong sense of public duty and she's  also i think a very lovely person but  she you know she is 95 and uh to be  working the kind of hours she works at  that age is quite extraordinary i think  it's a shame that the palace